From 9d4d509aad41536e37b0f4cf0caa2227631b576c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: legsmechanical <joshgaine@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 07:40:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] perf(manager,shim): remote-UI true push (F4) + non-blocking
 client fan-outs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two related responsivity changes for the overtake-tool remote UI:

1. Write/state mutex split + non-blocking fan-outs (manager). writeJSON held
   c.mu — the same mutex guarding subs and tool cursors — across the network
   write, so one wedged client could stall the tool ticker, the 5ms notify
   drain (overflowing the 64-entry shim ring), and the 30s backstop for up to
   the 5s write timeout. ruClient now has a dedicated writeMu for conn writes;
   periodic fan-outs dispatch via writeJSONTry (TryLock + goroutine, at most
   one in-flight write per client, drop-and-retry-next-tick semantics — all
   pushed values are absolute) and one-shot tool_info(gone) via writeJSONAsync.
   Cursor updates now happen only when a dispatch is accepted, so a dropped
   client stays stale and is retried next tick.

2. F4 push: shim probes the overtake DSP's cheap rui_poll digest IN-PROCESS
   every 4th SPI frame (post-transfer, where param serves already run; RT-safe:
   no alloc/log/IO) and pushes changes into the existing web param notify ring.
   Rev changes push immediately; playhead-only changes every 8th probe (~96ms).
   Unsupported modules (get_param < 0) are latched off until the next overtake
   load. The manager's notifyLoop routes these entries to a toolKick channel
   (never forwards them raw); toolTickLoop services kicks immediately with the
   pushed digest (zero shm reads on the push path) and, while pushes are fresh
   (<15s), relaxes its own rui_poll poll to a 2s backstop. Edit latency drops
   from the ~100ms poll cadence to ~12ms, and steady polling traffic on the
   contended shadow_param channel disappears. Full poll behavior is retained
   as fallback for an old shim or absent notify ring.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015f8H1BbPTkWyhPv2zphzhR
