 =?UTF-8?q?=20exemptions?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- serviceToolClients' needFull path advanced toolLastOn without ever sending
  rui_play (snapshots don't carry the on flag) — a play-state edge coinciding
  with a rev bump (any hardware stop during active modulation) was swallowed
  FOREVER and the browser playhead free-ran indefinitely. The rui_play frame
  now rides along with the snapshot when an edge is pending; on a dropped
  dispatch the cursor is left stale and the retry cadence delivers it.
- handleSubscribeTool consumes the arrival edge BEFORE its first network
  write: the client becomes ticker-visible at toolSub=true, so the ticker
  could win the markToolPresent race mid-seed and announce a second
  custom_ui, reloading the just-built iframe.
- The 300ms edit-quiet window now exempts _ruisel / transport / _cc_focus:
  for those the snapshot IS the requested data (newly selected clip, focused
  CC lane), not an echo — arming quiet just made the client's own request lag.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015f8H1BbPTkWyhPv2zphzhR
